  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Tinophylloloside may interact with HEp-2 cells through a series of target-mediated pathways. The drug is predicted to target Endoplasmic reticulum aminopeptidase 2, which in turn is targeted by (2S,4R)-4-hydroxypiperidine-2-carboxylic acid and 2-Phenyl-hex-5-en-3-ol, both of which have a known target of HEp-2. Additionally, Tinophylloloside is also predicted to target Annexin A1, which is targeted by a complex compound that ultimately targets HEp-2. These findings collectively indicate that Tinophylloloside may exert its effects on HEp-2 through multiple downstream pathways, potentially involving enzymatic activities in the endoplasmic reticulum and other cellular compartments. The evidence is consistent across different scoring models, suggesting a plausible biological relationship, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be elucidated.",
